---
description: Never use jq to filter or search SQL/API results
alwaysApply: true
---

# No jq Filtering on Query Results

NEVER pipe `snow sql` (or any data-fetching command) into `jq` with filtering functions (`select`, `map(select(...))`, `test`, `contains`, `any`, `all`). These silently return empty results when the filter is wrong, making missing data indistinguishable from a bad query.

## Correct workflow

1. Fetch raw results to see what you're working with: `snow sql -c <conn> --format json -q "..." `
2. Inspect the output structure visually
3. Only THEN extract known fields with simple jq paths (e.g. `jq '.[0].field'`)

## Allowed jq usage

- Pretty-print: `jq '.'`
- Extract a specific field you've already confirmed exists: `jq '.[0].name'`
- Format output: `jq -r '.[] | .name'`

## Forbidden jq usage

- `jq '.[] | select(.field == "value")'`
- `jq 'map(select(.x | test("pattern")))'`
- `jq '[.[] | select(.status == "RUNNING")]'`
- Any filtering before you've seen the raw data
